T*
(inn door, his sea-chest following behind him in a hand-barrow--a) Tj
T*
(tall, strong, heavy, nut-brown man, his tarry pigtail falling over the) Tj
T*
(shoulder of his soiled blue coat, his hands ragged and scarred, with) Tj
T*
(black, broken nails, and the sabre cut across one cheek, a dirty, livid) Tj
T*
(white. I remember him looking round the cove and whistling to himself) Tj
T*
(as he did so, and then breaking out in that old sea-song that he sang so) Tj
T*
(often afterwards:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
